CM_ "Porsche 986/996 powertrain CAN (CAN1 of the VCU), 500 kbit/s. Reverse engineering master; mirrored by tools/generate_can_md.py. Cycle (resolved #10, logs 2026-11-19): original DME and VCU both send 0x280, 0x289, 0x298, 0x7A0, 0x4E0 back to back every 10 ms in this order (VCU mean 10.00 ms, p99 10.45 ms). Driving logs can_logs/20261119_fahrt1/2 cover braking, steering and indicators. Original-DME reference can_logs/986_log_stand.csv was recorded with the engine off: its DME frames never change (coolant raw 0, RPM 0 or 4000 constant). OPEN (986 #11): no log yet with cruise control/steering-wheel buttons, lights/dimmer operated, hazard lights or an ABS stop. OPEN (986 #13): 20261119_stand shows two VCU send gaps (90.94-91.03 s with other frames still logged, 256.48-256.56 s with nothing logged); cause unknown.";
CM_ BO_ 640 "0x280. Sent by the VCU instead of the DME every 10 ms. RPM scaling matches Teensy (raw = rpm*4). Original DME (engine off) sends only 00 79 00 00 61 00 54 1C; bit 4 does not toggle (set once together with bit 23 and RPM 4000 in a later segment of the log, probably a tester mode). VCU sends 00 69 .. .. 61 60 54 1C: byte 1 lacks bit 12 and byte 5 is 0x60 (ThrottlePosition 37.5 %) instead of 0x00. OPEN (986 #6): meaning of bytes 1, 4, 6, 7 (VW PQ Motor_1: inner torque, inner torque without intervention, mechanical loss torque, driver torque request) needs the original DME at different pedal positions with the engine running; whether the VCU should copy byte 1 bit 12 and byte 5 = 0 is open.";
CM_ BO_ 649 "0x289. Sent by the VCU instead of the DME. Layout from VW PQ Motor_2. Bit 24 always 1, bit 25 = speed limiter selected (VCU code). Byte 0 multiplexed by MO2_Mp_Code (resolved #12): original DME and VCU send 0x00, 0x40, 0x80, 0xF3. Original holds the mux values 4/4/4/5 frames (170 ms), the VCU 4/4/4/4; original byte 3 = 0x7D, VCU 0x7C (bit 24 not sent; the VCU sets bit 24 in 0x298 instead, original 0x298 byte 3 = 0x00) - OPEN (986 #14): align the VCU with the original.";
CM_ BO_ 664 "0x298. Sent by the VCU instead of the DME. Several signals marked 'Turbo? Unsure' in the notes; Speed_raw scaling unknown.";
CM_ BO_ 680 "0x2A8. Wheel speeds, legacy 15-bit variant. Stationary log only: values not verified while driving.";
CM_ BO_ 416 "0x1A0. Bremse_1 (BR1) mapping (resolved #1, #12, logs 2026-11-19): byte 6 is an 8-bit message counter (former BR1_MSR_Mo), byte 7 lateral acceleration (former BR1_Zaehler, ASR_ESP, ESPASR_passive, Sta_ESP, Ersatz_Kmh). BR1_MSR_Anf is 0 in all logs, so the VW PQ multiplexed BR1_MSR_Mo_inv on byte 5 is dropped. Bytes 0, 4, 5 and bit 13 change only during ASR events (fahrt2 502.4 s, 835.4 s; fahrt1 67.8, 106.9, 131.2 s); no ABS stop logged yet. Power-on self test sets the lamp bits 8-10 and byte 7 = 0x00 for about 1 s.";
CM_ BO_ 1185 "0x4A1. Four 16-bit words with an 11-bit wheel pulse counter each (resolved #2, #3, logs 2026-11-19): +1 per about 41.8 mm, wraps at 2048, all 0 at standstill; increment vs vehicle speed r = 0.9997. Bits 11, 12, 27, 28, 43, 44, 59, 60 always 0. Bits 13-15 frame counter; bits 30-31/45-47/61-63 an 8-bit millisecond time stamp (hi*64 + mid*8 + lo, +100/101 per frame, also at standstill). Driver braking is not in this message (see 0x1A0 BR1_Lichtschalt). OPEN (986 #3): front/rear assignment of the pulse counters (left/right clear) and meaning of bit 29.";
CM_ BO_ 1248 "0x4E0. Sent by the VCU instead of the DME. Byte 0 status/lamp interpretation on bits 0..7 plus MO5 lamp/consumption layout on bits 9..31.";
CM_ BO_ 1296 "0x510. Bits 24-27 4-bit counter, bits 28-31, byte 4 and byte 7 always 0. Indicator bits blink with 0.66 s period (0.34 s on). OPEN (986 #4): bits 40 and 43 always 1 in all logs incl. start-up; bit 45 set only in 986start and the first 4 s of 20261119_stand (before an ignition cycle); Tempomat and steering-wheel buttons never seen set.";
CM_ BO_ 1312 "0x520. Byte 0 always 0x01; bytes 6-7 always 0 (VW PQ Kombi_3 odometer layout 40|20 refuted). Byte 5 is a 4-slot multiplex (Kombi_Mux bits 40-41, 6 data bits, 100 ms per slot, 400 ms cycle); slot 0 counts +1 per km (14 steps in fahrt1/fahrt2, 0.989 km per step against BR1_Rad_kmh), values carry on across logs. OilPressure 0xFF in all logs (not available). OPEN (986 #5): weights of slots 1-3 (64/4096/262144 assumed: 20 952 km at the end of fahrt2) and total vs trip odometer - compare with an odometer photo; meaning of byte 2.";
CM_ BO_ 1088 "0x440. PRND mapping from notes: P=128, R=119, N=96, D=81, M=225. Not present in any log incl. the drives 2026-11-19 (resolved #9): the car has no Tiptronic control unit on CAN.";
CM_ BO_ 192 "0x0C0. RB Lenkwinkel_1 layout: DLC=2, angle bits 5-15 as signed 11-bit value (two's complement, the former sign bit 15 is its MSB) plus status/check bits. Fahrt2: raw -218..216, continuous through zero, r = -0.94 with the rear wheel speed difference of 0x2A8. OPEN (986 #15): scale 2.5 deg/bit (+-545 deg) and sign (+ = right turn assumed) not verified at full lock.";
CM_ BO_ 1272 "0x4F8. Not present in any log, original DME included (resolved #8); the VCU does not send it either.";
CM_ BO_ 1376 "0x560. Not present in any log incl. the drives 2026-11-19 (resolved #8).";
CM_ BO_ 1952 "0x7A0. Sent by the VCU instead of the DME (raw bytes). Signals unknown. Standard payload: 85 0C 00 03 00 00 FF 02 (constant in the log).";
CM_ SG_ 640 RPM "Engine speed shown by the tachometer; the VCU sends the motor power here (VCU-REQ-005).";
CM_ SG_ 649 MO2_Kuehlm_T "Coolant temperature gauge; the VCU sends the inverter/motor temperature.";
CM_ SG_ 649 MO2_BLS "Brake light switch.";
CM_ SG_ 649 MO2_Sta_GRA "Cruise control status.";
CM_ SG_ 649 MO2_Bit24_Const "Always 1 in the stationary log; meaning unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 649 MO2_SpeedLimiter_Selected "Speed limiter selected (VCU field motor2_speed_limiter_selected); not in the original DBC.";
CM_ SG_ 664 Speed_raw "Scaling unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 1248 MO5_Heissl "Coolant overheat warning lamp.";
CM_ SG_ 1248 MO5_Verbrauch "Fuel consumption counter (15 bit); the VCU simulates consumption (VCU-REQ-006).";
CM_ SG_ 416 BR1_Rad_kmh "Reference vehicle speed (VCU field vref_kmh).";
CM_ SG_ 416 BR1_Querbeschl "Lateral acceleration (PSM sensor), + = left turn; r = 0.88 with the lateral acceleration from the 0x2A8 wheel speeds (fahrt2), none with longitudinal. About 0x7D at standstill, 0x00 while initialising. Scale/offset estimated - OPEN (986 #1): verify in a steady corner.";
CM_ SG_ 1185 Radimpulse_VL "Cumulative wheel pulse counter, ~41.8 mm per count, wraps at 2048 (front/rear OPEN, 986 #3).";
CM_ SG_ 1185 ABS2_Zaehler "Frame counter, +1 per 100 ms frame.";
CM_ SG_ 1185 ABS2_Init_OK "0 only in the first frame after ABS power-up (986start 14.85 s); meaning assumed.";
CM_ SG_ 1185 ABS2_Zeit_hi "Time stamp t = hi*64 + mid*8 + lo in ms, +100/101 per frame.";
CM_ SG_ 1296 InstrCluster1_Counter "4-bit frame counter, found in the stationary log 2026-11-11.";
CM_ SG_ 1312 InstrCluster2_Byte2_Unknown "Whole byte: 78..80 changing by +-1 in 986_log_stand, 0xFF in all VCU logs (sensor removed?); fuel level or oil temperature suspected (986 #5).";
CM_ SG_ 1312 Odometer_km_0 "Odometer slot 0, +1 per km (verified fahrt1/fahrt2).";
CM_ SG_ 1312 AmbientTemp "Plausible against the BMS cell temperatures (8-9 degC, 20261119_stand); not checked with a thermometer.";
CM_ SG_ 1312 LightDimmer "Only 0 and 100 seen: 0 for about 20 s after wake-up and at shutdown.";
CM_ SG_ 1296 VehicleSpeed "Displayed speed: about BR1_Rad_kmh + 4 km/h, lag about 0.4 s (fahrt1/fahrt2); max raw 517 (129 km/h).";
CM_ SG_ 1296 InstrCluster1_Bit14_Valid "0 for about 1 s after cluster start, then 1; speed-valid flag suspected (was decoded as part of VehicleSpeed with offset -4100).";
CM_ SG_ 1296 Indicator_Left "Left/right supported by the wheel speed difference in turns (fahrt2).";
CM_ SG_ 1296 InstrCluster1_Bit45 "See OPEN (986 #4).";
CM_ SG_ 640 PedalPosition1 "Not used in Teensy.";
CM_ SG_ 640 PedalPosition2 "Not used in Teensy.";
CM_ SG_ 649 MO2_Mp_Code "Byte 0 multiplexer: 0x00, 0x40, 0x80, 0xF3 for values 0-3.";
CM_ SG_ 649 MO2_CAN_Vers "Active when MO2_Mp_Code=0.";
CM_ SG_ 649 MO2_Motor_Code "Active when MO2_Mp_Code=1.";
CM_ SG_ 649 MO2_Getr_Code "Active when MO2_Mp_Code=2.";
CM_ SG_ 649 MO2_max_Mo "Active when MO2_Mp_Code=3; original DME sends raw 51 (510 Nm).";
